Review comment:

- [P2] Preserve origin IDs before matching final witnesses — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/base/abci/abcStmap_64.c:610-611
  When the downstream flow runs `topo`/`buffer` (or `stmap64 -s`), the network is duplicated with `Abc_NtkDupDfs`, which does not carry `vOrigNodeIds`. Since this loop only matches witnesses through `Abc_Stmap64MappedObjAigId()`, those common paths make every recorded witness look unmatched (`final-node = -1`) even if the node survived, so the new final-witness diagnostic is misleading after the intended buffering/sizing flow.
